	<strings name="main_menu/settings_select/player_setup/player_profile_edit/video_settings/frame_rate/performance_tools/help_strings">
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Shows how the game runs, at the bottom right. Simple is the frame rate: green is 30 or more, red under 30. Detailed adds the frame time, the 1% low, and the milliseconds spent on the GPU, the render thread, the game and waiting for the display."/>
		<string text="Times the game's own work (AI, objects, effects, scripts...) and, with Vulkan, each graphics setting's passes on the GPU, shown in the Detailed overlay with counts of objects and effects. Off times nothing."/>
		<string text="Saves a log of each frame's times beside every demo recorded, lined up with the demo's ticks, so a hitch seen in play can be found in the demo. The demo itself is unchanged."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="What the benchmark measures. Uncapped turns VSync, Variable Refresh and the frame cap off for the run: what your computer can draw. Your Settings keeps them: what you see as you play."/>
		<string text="The map the benchmark plays, of the multiplayer maps you have. Compare results only from the same map, bots and player: the results name all three."/>
		<string text="How many bots fight in the benchmark's match. A map takes only as many as suit it: 40 on the big maps, 16 on Hang 'Em High, 8 on Longest. The results say how many played."/>
		<string text="Who plays the view measured. Bot plays as the other bots do, the same match every run. Scripted is the walker of earlier results, to compare with them; it differs a little from run to run."/>
		<string text="Plays a fixed minute of the Benchmark Map with its bots, then shows the average frame rate, the 1% low, the frame times, the GPU and CPU time and your settings, and saves them in the benchmarks folder.|From the main menu only."/>
	</strings>
</menus>
